reuse-helper.bodyMarkdown:
After a helper owns a responsibility, other functions should usually call it rather than copy its implementation.

Avoid duplicating the cleanup rule:

```python
def clean_name(name):
    return name.strip().title()

def greeting(name):
    nice_name = name.strip().title()
    return "Hello, " + nice_name
```

Instead, reuse the helper:

```python
def clean_name(name):
    return name.strip().title()

def greeting(name):
    nice_name = clean_name(name)
    return "Hello, " + nice_name
```

The behavior stays the same, but the cleanup responsibility now has one source. If the cleanup rule changes later, only `clean_name` needs to change.
